    "body": "**Description:**\r\nFor a stand-alone setup, I used a laptop hosting an a-frame webpage and an Oculus Quest.\r\nThe loading of the page takes ages when no (real) internet is available.\r\nIt occurred to me that for a-text elements, fonts are being downloaded from the web. Also the oculus controller models don't load when no internet is available.\r\n\r\nI think a better way of hosting these can be found, or a way to run a-frame without internet should be documented\r\n\r\n- A-Frame Version: Not sure, the version that was available in July 2022\r\n- Platform / Device: Oculus Quest (with Firefox Reality Browser or Wolvic Reality Browser)\r\n- Reproducible Code Snippet or URL:\r\n`https://cdn.aframe.io/fonts/Roboto-msdf.json`\r\n\r\n\r\n",
